ADR-0012 says `tess init` and the first `tess sync` warn when the remote is public, since issues are exactly as private as the remote. Deferred past loop 2 (design session, 2026-11-20) because "public" needs a definition that does not need the network: a remote URL alone does not say whether a GitHub repository is public, and sync must stay usable offline. Options when picked up: a `gh`-style API probe only under `tess doctor --remote`; a one-time note in `tess init` that says where the issues will live and lets the user decide; or treating any `https://github.com/` remote as possibly public and saying so once.